  "command": "CC='/usr/bin/cc' CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL='1' LEAN_BRIDGE_NATIVE_TEST_GLIBC_FLOOR='2.36' LEAN_BRIDGE_NESTED_CHECKED_RECORD_WIT_MAX_LOAD='20' LEAN_BRIDGE_NESTED_CHECKED_RECORD_WIT_MODES='full,result-only' LEAN_BRIDGE_NESTED_CHECKED_RECORD_WIT_OUTPUT='/app/build/vo1511-nested-record-wit-b8ed8f9/records' LEAN_BRIDGE_NESTED_CHECKED_RECORD_WIT_ROUTES='ordinary,reviewed' LEAN_BRIDGE_NESTED_CHECKED_RECORD_WIT_TEST='1' LEAN_BRIDGE_WASM_TOOLS='/app/.toolchains/wasm-tools/bin/wasm-tools' LEAN_BRIDGE_WASMTIME_C_API='/app/.toolchains/wasmtime42' LEAN_NUM_THREADS='1' OMP_NUM_THREADS='1' MAKEFLAGS='-j1' 'taskset' '-c' '3' 'nice' '-n' '19' 'ionice' '-c' '3' 'node' '--max-old-space-size=3072' '--test' '--test-concurrency=1' '--test-reporter=tap' 'tests/helpers/nested-checked-record-wit-installed-tests.mjs'",
  "scope": "Two independent author builds reproduce the complete WIT component handoff. Author roots are removed before offline installation; the unchanged public C caller is compiled once, its source is removed, and the resulting executable runs before and after moving the complete installed tree, giving two executions per selection. The standalone result-only API projects checked-record payloads through Array and Option results without checked-input metadata. Checked-record WIT/WASI acceptance covers the established top-level Interval, Sized 3 and Bounded 0 101 forms plus the tested acyclic Packet, Holder and Choice forms through Array, List, Option, Product and Except copied positions. Generic, recursive and inherited checked records, other index kinds, open dependent or zero-payload records, callbacks and owned positions remain unreviewed. Both author routes and full/result-only APIs reproduce complete WIT component archives from two author roots, remove author roots, install offline, compile one unchanged public C caller, remove its source, and execute it before and after physically relocating each installation. The compiler-free runs use Wasmtime 42.0.1 and wasm-tools 1.245.1 on Linux x64/glibc 2.36 with an explicit 2.36 package floor, 64-bit native machine words and a recorded 20.0 host-load admission ceiling. The component requires its packaged native Lean host and is not a standalone WASI command. The archive retains complete handoff archives, extracted package records, receipts, installed inventories, execution records and both producer and verifier source closures. GCC, wasm-tools and Wasmtime remain trusted toolchain inputs. Hosted glibc 2.38 release-floor acceptance remains assigned to the dedicated workflow. Constructor dispatch and peak memory are unmeasured.",
