  "path": "ordinary-source",
  "scope": "Two independent author builds reproduce the complete WIT component handoff. Author roots are removed before offline installation; the unchanged public C caller is compiled once, its source is removed, and the resulting executable runs before and after moving the complete installed tree, giving two executions per selection. The full API checks direct and repeated parameters, Array, List, Option, Product, both Except branches, Holder.packet and the active Choice packet value field, including exact per-site constructors, normalization, complete rejected-input snapshots and recovery. Checked-record WIT/WASI acceptance covers the established top-level Interval, Sized 3 and Bounded 0 101 forms plus the tested acyclic Packet, Holder and Choice forms through Array, List, Option, Product and Except copied positions. Generic, recursive and inherited checked records, other index kinds, open dependent or zero-payload records, callbacks and owned positions remain unreviewed. Both author routes and full/result-only APIs reproduce complete WIT component archives from two author roots, remove author roots, install offline, compile one unchanged public C caller, remove its source, and execute it before and after physically relocating each installation. The compiler-free runs use Wasmtime 42.0.1 and wasm-tools 1.245.1 on Linux x64/glibc 2.36 with an explicit 2.36 package floor, 64-bit native machine words and a recorded 20.0 host-load admission ceiling. The component requires its packaged native Lean host and is not a standalone WASI command. The archive retains complete handoff archives, extracted package records, receipts, installed inventories, execution records and both producer and verifier source closures. GCC, wasm-tools and Wasmtime remain trusted toolchain inputs. Hosted glibc 2.38 release-floor acceptance remains assigned to the dedicated workflow. Constructor dispatch and peak memory are unmeasured.",
  "hostTypes": {
    "checked-record": {
      "field": "WIT record with list<u32> digit and word fields nested inside a Holder record and the packet case of a Choice variant; no proof field"
    }
  },
  "conversionNotes": {
    "checked-record": "Pass the generated record's runtime payload fields, without proof values. The selected Lean constructor checks each input and may normalize it; rejection identifies the parameter and constructor and preserves caller data. Results contain copied payload fields with proofs erased. Both ordinary and independently reviewed packages, including standalone result-only packages, passed installed checks. The tested Component Model Packet is a WIT record whose Fin 10 digit and checked Nat Subtype word are canonical list<u32> limbs. A Holder record nests Packet, and the packet case of Choice carries it in its active branch. Generated WIT adapters apply the exact Packet and nested Word constructors selected at each direct, repeated, Array, List, Option, Product, Except, Holder and Choice input site. Rejected calls preserve the complete caller value tree and output sentinel, and later valid calls recover. Packet arrays and options returned by Lean contain proof-free WIT records without input-constructor selections."
  },
